---
to: "lib/support_desk/<%= String.downcase(domain_name) %>.ex"
for_each: domains
mode: file
---
<% resources_in_domain = Enum.filter(domain_resources, &(&1["domain_module"] == domain_module)) %>
defmodule <%= domain_module %> do
  @moduledoc """
  Ash.Domain registering every resource in the ash-lifecycle-pack fixture
  whose ontology-declared `alp:resourceDomain` really resolves to THIS
  domain module (`<%= domain_module %>`).

  Manufactured by ggen_igniter from the admitted alp: ontology -- do not
  hand-edit; regenerate from the ontology instead. FIXED (multi-domain
  admission gap): this template used to assume a SINGLE domain module via
  `domain_resources |> List.first() |> Map.get("domain_module")`, so any
  resource whose real declared domain differed from the pack's one assumed
  domain got silently misregistered under the wrong module. It now fans out
  one real domain module PER distinct domain the ontology actually declares
  (`for_each: domains`, driven by `gates/055_domains.rq`'s
  `SELECT DISTINCT ?domain_name ?domain_module` over every resource's real
  `alp:resourceDomain`), and each rendering filters the full
  `gates/050_domain_resources.rq` result set (bound here as
  `domain_resources`) down to only the rows whose own `domain_module` matches
  THIS render's domain -- so a resource is registered under its real
  declared domain, never folded under whichever row happened to sort first.
  This template fully regenerates the whole module from scratch on every run
  (mode: file, same idempotent-regeneration convention as resource.ex.eex)
  rather than injecting into an existing file: `GgenIgniter.Actuate.inject_content!/5`
  exists in this codebase but `Mix.Tasks.GgenIgniter.Sync` never calls it for
  `mode: file` templates (only `Actuate.write_file!/3`), so AST-patch/inject
  wiring is not actually exercised on this path -- regenerating the whole
  small module avoids depending on machinery that isn't wired here.
  """

  use Ash.Domain

  resources do
<%= for d <- resources_in_domain do %>    resource(<%= d["resource_module"] %>)
<% end %>  end
end
